    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` (later than the server date) with a 400 response, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 thrown when a supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with body `{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`, matching the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` shape.\n\n3. **`officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n4. **`ValidateNewOwner`** \u2014 added the guard in the existing validation step (registration date is optional; when supplied it may be back-dated but never into the future), and declared the new checked exception on the `service` method.\n\nThe check lives in the first pipeline step (`ValidateNewOwner`), so an invalid future date is rejected before any owner is built or persisted. The new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` passes and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
